of May 2017 at the Manchester Arena  22 people were murdered  and over 1 000 injured in a planned  indiscriminate  and cowardly Act of abject barbarity  today our thoughts  are with bereaved families and the  survivors who have been Central to  everything we have done  since this attack took place  this inquiry set out to leave no stone  unturned in its effort to provide  answers about what happened on the night  of the attack  the comprehensive report that we have  received this morning  records the very detailed summation of  Sir John Saunders findings and is the  embodiment of the Care taken by him to  fulfill its purpose  we recognize that many aspects of the  latest published volume  will make for difficult and distressing  reading for those most affected  on behalf of Grace Manchester please I  thank the inquiry team for the  opportunities that we have been given  to participate fully and fairly in the  inquiry process and we welcome today's  report  I fully accept the findings of the chair  Sir John Saunders  Beyond the selflessness and  professionalism of so many of our  Frontline staff it is also clear  that our coordination of the response to  this atrocity was poor  we have failed to plan effectively and  the execution of that which was planned  was simply not good enough  our actions were substantially  inadequate and fell short of what the  public have every right to expect  and for this I apologize unreservedly  our failure to affect proper command and  control of the incident from the outset  undermined an effective multi-agency  response to a dreadful set of  circumstances  we did not act upon learning from  previous exercises which could have  produced the burden or impact felt on  the force duty officer  for communications per planning  inadequate training and shortcomings in  strategic leadership all played a part  in our failure  all of these failings could and should  have been identified and mitigated  through learning from robustly designed  t